# PERMISSIONS

Use centralized permissions.

Examples:

boards.view
boards.create
boards.update
boards.delete

faces.view
faces.create
faces.update
faces.delete

compliance.view
compliance.manage

occupancy.view
occupancy.manage

enquiries.view
enquiries.manage

field.view
field.manage

team.manage

settings.manage

audit.view

See `docs/PERMISSIONS.md` for the full matrix.

---

# AUTHORIZATION

Every sensitive operation requires:

1. authenticated user
2. organization membership
3. appropriate permission
4. target resource belongs to authorized tenant

Never rely on route protection alone.

`lib/supabase/proxy.ts` gates routes. It is not sufficient authorization for mutations.

---

# IDOR PROTECTION

Never assume that knowing:

/boards/123

means the user may access board 123.

Always verify authorization server-side.

RLS must deny Tenant B rows even if the UUID is known.

---

# PUBLIC MARKETPLACE

Public users can only access explicitly public marketplace data.

Use `marketplace_listings` and `marketplace_photos` views.

Never return:

- internal notes
- customer data
- contracts
- private documents
- tenant metadata
- internal pricing information (`floor_rate` is internal)
- internal operational information

---

# AUDIT

Important mutations must generate audit records.

Use `public.write_audit_log(...)`.

At minimum:

create
update
delete
publish
unpublish
occupancy changes
compliance changes
enquiry changes
field completion
proof upload

---

# SECURITY TESTING

Every tenant-owned feature should have a test verifying:

Tenant A cannot access Tenant B.

This is mandatory.
